# Compose Screen Conventions

```kotlin
@Composable
fun FooScreen(
    onNavigateBack: () -> Unit,
    viewModel: FooViewModel = hiltViewModel()
) {
    val uiState by viewModel.uiState.collectAsStateWithLifecycle()

    when (val state = uiState) {
        FooUiState.Loading -> MezonLoadingScreen()
        FooUiState.Empty -> MezonEmptyScreen(icon = ..., message = "...")
        is FooUiState.Error -> MezonErrorScreen(
            message = state.message,
            onRetry = { viewModel.onIntent(FooIntent.Load) }
        )
        is FooUiState.Success -> { /* content */ }
    }
}
```

## Rules

- Always use `collectAsStateWithLifecycle()` (not `collectAsState`)
- Navigation callbacks are lambda params: `onNavigateBack`, `onOpenChat`, `onLogout`
- ViewModel via `hiltViewModel()`
- Use `MezonLoadingScreen`, `MezonErrorScreen`, `MezonEmptyScreen` for standard states
- Private composables for sub-components: `@Composable private fun FooItem(...)`
- `when (uiState)` must be exhaustive — handle all sealed branches including `Empty`
- LazyColumn items must have unique `key` and `contentType`

## Chat screen: LazyColumn with reverseLayout (zero-allocation)

```kotlin
LazyColumn(
    modifier = Modifier.fillMaxSize(),
    state = listState,
    reverseLayout = true
) {
    items(
        count = messages.size,
        key = { messages[messages.size - 1 - it].id },
        contentType = { if (messages[messages.size - 1 - it].isMe) 0 else 1 }
    ) { index ->
        MessageBubble(messages[messages.size - 1 - index])
    }
}
```

- Use index-based `items(count)` — zero allocation (no `asReversed()`)
- `derivedStateOf` for load-more trigger and jump-to-bottom
- Auto-scroll on new messages only when already at bottom
- Use `remember(msg.content) { parseContentText(msg.content) }` in MessageBubble
